9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"576424a1f399625399b4bdc61a70b4293721a38a856d7ad90f027d675fbe7f39","event_uuid":"84579120-f3fb-4414-b16c-ead36412db76","position":{"commit_sha":"39977ce45e3c112bdf333b8893f02955b8890f85","position":"1787345187724297001-84579120-f3fb-4414-b16c-ead36412db76"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"3faea5cb957301fdc28e5f8d944c95d44d060f03605605ee656aa4919bf30d36","event_uuid":"7efd4d45-a7d9-4747-ae22-bb2c8061d31d","position":{"commit_sha":"07927404d278ef9b53a0f922c515e7d8aa4defa6","position":"1787345906646660001-7efd4d45-a7d9-4747-ae22-bb2c8061d31d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"10e874161f4448dc392cf4b332f86636ec1f2a008d8164ff9ceacef5d918de02","event_uuid":"04700704-2805-4466-88d1-83600b94a6f8","position":{"commit_sha":"82be38218efadecb38d60d78e133d865ca057079","position":"1787345911439511001-04700704-2805-4466-88d1-83600b94a6f8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787080906460373001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"6d71ef19-81cb-485d-bd82-ffef18793520","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"ba48-a88a-92bd-45d0"},{"link_uuid":"75a08925-f14f-4589-a9e4-e6887492bb90","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"37cc-ee47-4b90-4e22"},{"link_uuid":"d0a50165-a45f-40ee-bb5a-86122c626920","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"10a6-7fe2-4163-40f7"},{"link_uuid":"1aeb2e6c-ef67-498d-b069-b00cb3d8b903","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"f4d8-0558-b080-4905"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe review gates currently read effective criteria and routing through multiple seams. Code review then consults packaged-only overlay and detector registries, so a project disable or retune can be ignored and an activated project DET criterion can disappear. Separate reads can also describe different repository policy states. RP-06 requires one immutable authority before any selection or model call.\n\n## Approach\nCreate a repository-bound `CriteriaSnapshot` in `rebar.llm.criteria`. It compiles effective built-ins, project LLM criteria, project DET criteria, prompt/routing/posture/applicability metadata, source locations, and one deterministic digest from the provided repository root and already-resolved operation inputs. Consumers receive the snapshot; they do not reread ambient policy.\n\nKeep applicability vocabularies gate-specific. For project code-review LLM criteria, validate `applies_to` as a non-empty list of non-empty repository-relative globs and define `[\"**\"]` as repository-wide. `[\"**\"]` selects the criterion **unconditionally**, including for a review whose changed-files set is empty — this exactly reproduces the prior ungated `applies_to: []` short-circuit (`if not globs: return True`), so repository-wide never regresses to the `any(glob_match …)`-over-empty-`changed_files` = False edge. A scoped glob that matches no changed path produces a typed non-applicable selection reason. Built-in secondary triggers remain unchanged, project DET selection remains detector-owned, and plan review retains `applies_at` and `trigger`.\n\nWhere the new rule lives (do not regress the shared load contract): the existing shared `criteria/overlay.py::_validate_applies_to` deliberately permits an empty list as the \"ungated\" spelling and is called for BOTH gates (ADR 0074); it stays intact so plan-review project criteria (which carry no `applies_to`) and any other gate are unaffected. The stricter \"non-empty globs, `[\"**\"]` = repository-wide, unconditional-select\" rule is applied ONLY to `code_review` `project.`-prefixed LLM criteria, at snapshot-compile in the new `CriteriaSnapshot`/`overlay` code-review-gated path — not in the shared validator. Migrating `.rebar/criteria_routing.json` entry `project.review-phase-boundaries` from `[]` to `[\"**\"]` is precisely what keeps THIS repo's overlay legal under the new code-review rule while leaving its current all-review membership explicit and unchanged.\n\n### Alternatives / prior art\n`CriteriaSnapshot` is a **projection composed with**, not a duplicate of, the repo's existing immutable-authority machinery: ADR 0098's `OperationSnapshot` (an operation resolves one immutable, non-secret snapshot and never rereads ambient config) is the resolution-time authority this snapshot is derived under; ADR 0017 established the one shared `rebar.llm.criteria` delegation layer this story extends (delegation, not rip-and-replace); and `overlay.py::_overlay_signature` already computes a sha256 content digest feeding the per-`(gate, repo, signature)` memoized `_effective_routing_cached` immutable view. The `CriteriaSnapshot` digest **reuses/extends** that existing `_overlay_signature` content digest rather than inventing a parallel one. The reason a single effective authority is preferable to tightening the gate-specific registry reads in place: the current defects (a code-review project disable ignored, an activated project DET dropped, two reads describing different repository states) are exactly the cross-read divergences that survive in-place tightening — one compiled snapshot handed to consumers removes the divergent-read class structurally. The ADR records this comparison.\n\nRecord an ADR describing snapshot ownership, gate-specific applicability, the explicit global-glob spelling, and why a single effective authority is preferable to gate-specific registry reads. The snapshot is data and policy only; it does not interpret YAML/BPMN topology, execute criteria, or decide verdicts.\n\n## Migration and Rollback\nAdd the snapshot alongside existing registry readers. Golden contract tests compare the snapshot-derived selection inputs with current behavior when no project overlay is present and allow only the approved corrections for effective disables/retunes, project DET inclusion, and project LLM applicability. Existing registry APIs remain as compatibility adapters until the dependent cutover stories land; rollback is a code revert, not a new configuration flag.\n\n## Testing\nUse in-process unit and real producer-to-consumer contract tests. One tier lower is insufficient because the known defects occur between the overlay producer and packaged-routing consumers. Tests feed real project routing files through the loader and snapshot compiler, then assert exact selected policy, source provenance, and digest behavior. Negative controls cover built-in empty secondary triggers and plan-review routing, which must not adopt the new project-LLM glob rule. One contract case exercises the diverging empty-`changed_files` edge and asserts a `[\"**\"]` code-review project criterion still selects (proving the migration is behavior-preserving there).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] A real project overlay compiled through `CriteriaSnapshot` yields one immutable digest-bound view containing effective built-in, project LLM, and project DET policy with source provenance.\n- [x] A project code-review LLM criterion with an empty, missing, non-list, or blank `applies_to` fails before any model call with its criterion id, configuration location, and the remedy `use [\"**\"] for repository-wide`.\n- [x] Given root, nested, and dot changed paths, `applies_to: [\"**\"]` selects the criterion exactly once.\n- [x] `applies_to: [\"**\"]` selects the criterion unconditionally when `changed_files` is empty (the diverging edge), and a contract test asserts this empty-changed-files case selects, proving the `[]`→`[\"**\"]` migration preserves the prior ungated behavior.\n- [x] A nonmatching scoped glob records a typed non-applicable selection reason without executing the criterion.\n- [x] `.rebar/criteria_routing.json` declares `project.review-phase-boundaries.applies_to` as `[\"**\"]`.\n- [x] A contract test proves `project.review-phase-boundaries` review membership is unchanged by the `[]`→`[\"**\"]` migration, including the empty-changed-files case above.\n- [x] The shared `_validate_applies_to` empty-list-legal contract is left intact for plan-review project criteria (a negative-control test proves plan-review routing does not adopt the code-review non-empty-glob rule).\n- [x] Contract tests prove effective built-in disables/retunes are present in the snapshot.\n- [x] Contract tests prove activated project DET entries are present in the snapshot.\n- [x] A negative-control test proves built-in secondary-trigger semantics remain unchanged in the snapshot.\n- [x] An ADR documents snapshot ownership, digest inputs (its reuse of the existing `_overlay_signature` content digest), gate-specific applicability, the prior-art comparison against ADR 0098/0017, compatibility adapters, and the revert-based rollback.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/criteria/snapshot.py","reason":"New immutable effective-policy snapshot, digest, and the shared select_project_applicability helper."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/criteria/overlay.py","reason":"Shared overlay layer reused for signature/routing (validator left intact)."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/criteria/__init__.py","reason":"Expose the snapshot seam to review gates."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/code_review/registry.py","reason":"Delegate the code-review consumer project_criterion_applies to the shared applicability helper so the [] to [\"**\"] migration is behavior-preserving."},{"path":".rebar/criteria_routing.json","reason":"Migrate project.review-phase-boundaries to the explicit repository-wide glob."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_criteria_snapshot.py","reason":"Producer-to-consumer snapshot, digest, applicability, DET-exemption, and negative-control contracts."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_criteria_overlay.py","reason":"Located invalid-project-glob validation and the migration contract tests."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_project_review_phase_boundaries.py","reason":"Update the config-pinning test and docstring for the migrated repository-wide glob."},{"path":"docs/adr/0102-review-discovery-effective-policy.md","reason":"Architecture decision for the unified review-policy snapshot."},{"path":"docs/adr/.numbers/0102","reason":"ADR-number bijection marker for ADR 0102."},{"path":"docs/adr/README.md","reason":"Index the new ADR."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","58bd-d656-c52f-4cf4"],["relates_to","10a6-7fe2-4163-40f7"],["relates_to","37cc-ee47-4b90-4e22"],["relates_to","ba48-a88a-92bd-45d0"],["relates_to","f4d8-0558-b080-4905"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"58bd-d656-c52f-4cf4","parent_status_uuid":"7efd4d45-a7d9-4747-ae22-bb2c8061d31d","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["rp-06","llm","criteria","architecture"],"ticket_id":"60c1-80de-a22f-4d39","ticket_type":"story","title":"RP-06 S1 — Compile immutable effective review-policy snapshots","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["2aefa8e8-d1b8-4703-af3e-2d879596a56d","41ae5761-4fe5-42a5-860e-4f471e1e1d66","3579c189-d977-40a4-be03-737f7ccac610","a2ae35b0-8717-4fe7-9524-7b7a23b9fd13","75a08925-f14f-4589-a9e4-e6887492bb90","d0a50165-a45f-40ee-bb5a-86122c626920","1aeb2e6c-ef67-498d-b069-b00cb3d8b903","49c338a6-5071-49bf-a20a-f0008c6bcb9a","8cfbd9d0-e414-4ee5-a8a7-d7d7c0b25269","84579120-f3fb-4414-b16c-ead36412db76","7efd4d45-a7d9-4747-ae22-bb2c8061d31d","04700704-2805-4466-88d1-83600b94a6f8"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787354428781990001,"uuid":"b1143c3f-f1da-4308-a09d-44772603daba"}